# Dev-only defaults. Copy to .env (make does this). Never reuse these values outside local development.
FH_ENV=dev
FH_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=dev-postgres-superuser
FH_DB_OWNER_PASSWORD=dev-owner-password
FH_DB_APP_PASSWORD=dev-app-password
FH_DB_PLATFORM_PASSWORD=dev-platform-password
# Guards POST /api/v1/operator/tenants (tenant onboarding). Empty disables the endpoint.
FH_OPERATOR_TOKEN=dev-operator-token
# AES-256-GCM key (base64, 32 bytes) for replayable tenant secrets such as webhook signing keys. Unset in dev and
# test uses a built-in dev key; required everywhere else.
# FH_DATA_KEY=
# S3-compatible object storage (storage.adapter: s3). Dev values match the `s3` service (RustFS, MinIO-compatible)
# in `docker compose --profile storage`; unset falls back to boto3's default chain (an instance role).
# FH_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=dev-minio
# FH_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=dev-minio-secret
# Lane isolation for parallel checkouts (optional; defaults: facilityhub, facilityhub_test, 8100, 5183).
# Set all four in a lane's .env, then run `make lane-db`.
# FH_DB_NAME=facilityhub_space
# FH_TEST_DB_NAME=facilityhub_test_space
# FH_API_PORT=8110
# FH_WEB_PORT=5193
# TLS to Postgres and Redis (security-baseline V9): unset in dev and test (plain local containers). Required
# everywhere else: sslmode verify-full with PGSSLROOTCERT (read by libpq; FH_ENV=stack alone accepts require), and a
# rediss:// URL (it may carry the Redis password, so it lives here and never in a config file).
# FH_DB_SSLMODE=verify-full
# FH_REDIS_URL=rediss://:password@cache.internal:6380/0
# Stripe test mode (docs/dev/stripe-test-mode.md). Test-mode keys only: a live key (sk_live_, pk_live_, rk_live_)
# refuses to start unless FH_ENV is prod or production. Unset keeps the fake processor.
# FH_PAYMENTS_PROVIDER=stripe
# FH_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=rk_test_...
# FH_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# FH_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
